\]

Where:
- \( \text{VO}_2 \) is the volume of oxygen consumed per unit of time (e.g., mL/min).
- \( \text{VO}_2/V̇_e \) is the arteriovenous oxygen tension difference (AVOTD), which is the difference in oxygen tension between arterial and venous blood.

This formula is derived from Fick's equation, which relates the rate of oxygen consumption (\( \text{VO}_2 \)) to the arteriovenous oxygen tension difference (AVOTD) and the blood flow rate (\( V̇_b \)):

\[
\text{VO}_2 = \text{AVOTD} \times V_b
