","ATMIES is a protein that plays a crucial role in DNA repair during V(D)J recombination. This process is essential for the development of a functional immune system. During V(D)J recombination, the DNA sequences encoding the variable regions of the DNA repair genes are shuffled and combined randomly, generating a vast repertoire of unique protein sequences. This process is essential for the generation of a diverse immune system that can recognize and respond to a wide range of potential threats.

ATMIES is involved in the repair of the DNA intermediates generated during V(D)J recombination. These intermediates are highly mutagenic and can lead to genomic instability if not repaired correctly. ATMIES helps to maintain genome integrity by promoting the repair of these intermediates through the repair pathway. This ensures that the V(D)J recombination process proceeds accurately and generates functional immune cells.

