   - Calculate the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of the data.
   - Arrange the eigenvectors in decreasing order of their corresponding eigenvalues.
   - The eigenvectors represent the principal directions of variation in the data, and the eigenvalues represent the amount of variation explained by each eigenvector.

