ATMIES is involved in the repair of the DNA intermediates generated during V(D)J recombination. These intermediates are highly mutagenic and can lead to genomic instability if not repaired correctly. ATMIES helps to maintain genome integrity by promoting the repair of these intermediates through the repair pathway. This ensures that the V(D)J recombination process proceeds accurately and generates functional immune cells.

