- \(R\) is the gas constant (8.314 J/mol·K),
- \(T_b\) is the boiling point of water at 1 atm (373.15 K),
- \(P_1\) is the atmospheric pressure (1 atm),
- \(P_2\) is the pressure at the Atlantis II Deep (100 atm).

Substituting the values:
\[
\Delta T_b = \frac{8.314 \times 373.15}{1000} \left( \frac{100 - 1}{1} \right) = 31.0°C
\]

