1. Polarimetry: If the product is a racemic mixture, it will not rotate plane-polarized light. If the product is enantiomerically pure, it will rotate plane-polarized light in either a clockwise (dextrorotatory) or counterclockwise (levorotatory) direction. The magnitude of the rotation can be used to determine the enantiomeric excess (ee) of the product.

