1. Nutrient recycling: Biomass can be used as a source of nutrients for soil when it is returned to the land as organic matter. This can help maintain or improve soil fertility and increase the availability of essential nutrients like nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium. This can lead to a more balanced chemical composition and improved soil pH levels.

