Next, compute the values of $\cos (\frac{11 \pi}{2} - \alpha)$ and $\sin (\frac{1pi}{2} + \alpha)$:
- $\cos (\frac{11 \pi}{2} - \alpha) = \cos (\frac{\pi}{2} - \alpha) = \sin \alpha$
- $\sin (\frac{11 \pi}{2} + \alpha) = \sin (\frac{\pi}{2} + \alpha) = \cos \alpha$

