\[
n - 36 = 27 - 45 \quad \text{or} \quad n - 45 = 36 - 27.
\]
Solving these equations gives \( n = 36 \) or \( n = 68 \). However, the correct answer is \( \boxed{36} \), as the difference \( 27 - 45 = -18 \) is consistent with the other pair.

