","a) **Retrotemporal** (a retrospective study is a type of temporal study, which is a subset of temporal analysis. It is a method of analysis where the data is collected from a group of people at a specific point in time, and the researchers then study the relationship between the variables of interest and the events that have already happened to the group. In this case, the data is collected at a specific point in time, and the researchers are studying the relationship between smoking and the development of bladder cancer, which is an event that has already happened to the group. Thus, this is a retrospective study.)  
b) **Cross-sectional** (A cross-sectional study is a type of study that measures variables in a group of people at a specific point in time. In this case, the nurses' eating habits and general health are measured at the same time, so this is a cross-sectional study.)  
c) **Prospective** (A prospective study is a type of study that involves tracking a group of people over time to observe the development of a variable of interest. In this case, the team is tracking the eating and exercise patterns of the people and observing who is afflicted with cancer later in life, so this is a prospective study.)  
d) **No temporal component** (This is a non-temporal analysis, as it is not concerned with time or temporal relationships. The comparison of prices is made at a specific point in time, and the study does not involve tracking prices over time or comparing them to events that have occurred over time.)  

**Final Answer:**  
a) $\boxed{\text{Retrotemporal}}$  
b) $\boxed{\text{Cross-sectional}}$  
c) $\boxed{\text{Prospective}}$  
d) $\boxed{\text{No temporal component}}$
