1. As matter and radiation approach the event horizon, the boundary around a black hole through which nothing, not even light, can escape, their apparent speed to an outside observer increases to the speed of light. This is because the curvature of spacetime becomes so extreme that the apparent motion of the infalling matter and radiation appears to reach the speed of light, even if it was not moving at that speed initially.

